      "id": "arxiv:2610.15991",
      "date": "2026-10-11",
      "title": "Revocation Is Not Complete at Receipt: An Executable Outcome Contract for Distributed Agent-Tool Gateways",
      "topic": "agent",
      "language": [
        "zh",
        "en"
      ],
      "authors": [
        "Lifei Liu",
        "Haoran Yu",
        "Danping Zhang"
      ],
      "institution": "Nanchang Hangkong University",
      "summary": {
        "zh": "本文揭示了分布式智能体系统中“接收即撤销完成”这一假设的危险性。通过提出 C0-C5 有界结果契约，作者证明了必须将监控范围延伸至实际效果的预防阶段，才能准确判定撤销是否真正完成。实验表明，在网络异常或恶意配置下，传统的传输确认机制会掩盖严重的权限漏洞，而本文提出的契约机制能够提供零假阳性的准确审计结果，为分布式智能体安全提供了新的验证标准。",
        "en": "- **Background**: In distributed agent workflows, delegated authority is cached at tool gateways. Revocation status is often reported via issuer commit, transport acknowledgment, or receiver persistence."
      },
      "links": {
        "abs": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2610.15991v1",
